-- Spec EMIT-4 and EMIT-5: a chain of `&&` or `||` loads and runs at any
-- length, whatever its operands need: operands with statements of their
-- own (indexing, list comparison), mixed operators, an operand that must
-- not run once the chain is decided, an operand chain that reads a value
-- bound by an earlier operand, and 6000 operands that need no statements.
-- `andAt k` and `orAt k` are decided by their k-th of 40 operands, each a
-- call that raises if it runs after the deciding one, so k on either side
-- of every run boundary shows that a chain stops where it is decided.
module main (allIdx, anyIdx, shortCut, listEq, mixed, scoped, condLet, flat, andAt, orAt)

import root-py

